.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt YT 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm yt ,
.Nm if_yt
.Nd Motorcomm YT6801 Gigabit Ethernet driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in the
kernel configuration file:
.Bd -ragged -offset indent
.Cd "device pci"
.Cd "device ether"
.Cd "device miibus"
.Cd "device iflib"
.Cd "device yt"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if_yt_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides
.Xr iflib 4
support for the
Motorcomm YT6801 PCI Ethernet controller.
The controller uses a Synopsys DesignWare MAC 4 core.
The driver uses a single transmit queue and a single receive queue.
.Pp
The driver supports 10, 100, and 1000 Mbps operation in full-duplex mode.
Media selection and autonegotiation are handled by
.Xr miibus 4 .
Use
.Xr ifconfig 8
to select a media type supported by the attached PHY.
Half-duplex operation is not supported by this driver.
.Pp
Standard Ethernet MTUs up to 1500 bytes and VLAN-sized frames are supported.
VLAN tag insertion and removal are performed in software.
Jumbo frames, hardware checksum offloading, TCP segmentation offloading,
and receive-side scaling are not supported.
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the following PCI device:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Motorcomm YT6801 Gigabit Ethernet (vendor/device ID 1f0a:6801).
.El
The driver uses a single MSI message when the platform can allocate one,
with a shared interrupt for the transmit and receive queues.
It falls back to legacy INTx when MSI is unavailable or allocation fails.
MSI-X queue routing is not supported.
.Sh LOADER TUNABLES
The following tunable can be set in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bl -tag -width "hint.yt.%d.disable_msi"
.It Va hint.yt.%d.disable_msi
Set to a nonzero value to use legacy INTx instead of MSI for this unit.
The default is zero.
.El
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
The following read-only
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are available under
.Va dev.yt.%d ,
where
.Li %d
is the interface unit number:
.Bl -tag -width "last_host_irq"
.It Va interrupts
Number of handled device interrupts.
.It Va tx_errors
Number of transmit descriptors reporting an error.
.It Va rx_errors
Number of receive descriptors rejected for an error or invalid length.
.It Va resets
Number of successful DMA initializations.
.It Va last_status
DMA status recorded by the most recent handled interrupt.
.It Va last_tx
Status of the most recently reclaimed transmit descriptor.
.It Va last_rx
Status of the most recently examined receive descriptor.
.It Va rearm_pending
Number of times pending DMA work was found while interrupts were rearmed.
.It Va last_host_irq
Wrapper interrupt status recorded by the most recent handled interrupt.
.It Va mac_config
Current MAC configuration register.
.It Va dma_bus_mode
Current DMA bus mode register.
.It Va dma_status
Current DMA status register.
.It Va dma_irq_enable
Current DMA interrupt enable register.
.It Va dma_opmode
Current receive-channel control register.
.El
.Pp
Additional queue statistics and settings are provided by
.Xr iflib 4 .
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "yt%d: invalid firmware MAC address"
The address supplied by firmware is zero or a multicast address.
The device cannot attach.
.It "yt%d: TX error descriptor=%#x"
The hardware reported a transmit error.
The descriptor status is printed for the first error;
.Va dev.yt.%d.tx_errors
counts subsequent errors.
.It "yt%d: DMA reset timeout; bus mastering disabled"
The controller did not complete a DMA reset.
Bus mastering was disabled to prevent further DMA access.
.El
